{
  "case_id": "2007-07-21",
  "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Crawford et al.)",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case involves a law that directly burdens our most fundamental right, the right to vote. Those Indiana voters who lack the identification now required by the new photo ID law must overcome substantial practical and financial burdens before they can continue to exercise their constitutional right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first today in Case 07-21 and 07-25, Crawford v. Marion County Election Board and Indiana Democratic Party v. Secretary Rokita."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Before -- before we get to that, can we talk about standing a little? Who are the -- who are the complainants here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: As I understand it, though, Mr. Smith, the trial court didn't rely on, simply on the associational standing of the Democratic Party, did it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We have -- the record shows that fewer than 1 percent of people in Indiana don't have a photo ID."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Now, what's your response to that? Because that's their argument on the other side."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If this is not a problem at all, how do you account for the fact that the Commission on Federal Election Reform that was co-chaired by former President Carter and former Secretary of State Baker recommended a voter ID requirement, and many other countries around the world have voter ID requirements?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, you're telling us that, you know, we've got to be careful and it's difficult. But Justice Alito's question is: What are we supposed to look at, how are we supposed to do it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: And why, why can't the people injured by this law appear themselves and say the law can't be applied to us? You seem to accept that a facial challenge is appropriate here. Why is -- some different kind of a facial challenge. I thought in the usual facial challenge you have to show that there is no situation in which the law cannot be constitutionally applied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Indiana",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Indiana voter registration application, all a person has to do to register is to write in, enclose a utility bill that has his name and address, and if he doesn't have a photo ID, he can write the four numbers of his Social Security; and if he doesn't have that either he doesn't have to do anything, and they will give him a number -- and you mail it in. And you're registered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Don't you need a birth certificate to get a passport?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0003-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: But, conversely, nowhere\nis it -- nowhere is it a rational assumption that all 32\nof these individuals has a great claim. It may be that\nsome of them are people who just forgot their ID --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: If we did that, I assume\nchallenges could be made in advance of the election."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: That is true, and there is\na provision for judicial review under Indiana law, of\nthe provisional ballots, if there's an ongoing dispute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-07-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0a287ec028c7dc052743647dbeb1e46fdb1344f9ce5a7f3307c7c81d2d228fda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a287ec028c7-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
